INT. DECOMMISSIONED PLANETARIUM - NIGHT

A dome of peeling white plaster. Stars projected from a rusted machine that still works. Seats torn, upholstery leaking foam. Pigeons roost in the rafters.

NOOR HAKIM, 30s, field agent, black jacket, hair tied back, crouches behind a row of seats. Pistol drawn. She is bleeding from the shoulder.

ELLISON "DOC" BRAGG, 50s, ex-surgeon turned smuggler, kneels beside the projector with a bag of surgical tools. He is calm.

RAFE TOLLIVER, 30s, tall, in a stained suit, lies on the central floor, one hand pressed to his ribs. His gun is three feet from his fingers.

Silence. Stars wheel overhead.

NOOR
Doc, back off.

DOC
Noor, I'm trying to help.

NOOR
By what? Selling him a bandage?

Doc raises both hands. Rafe groans.

RAFE
Noor.

NOOR
Don't talk.

RAFE
Noor. Look at me.

She crosses to him. Kicks the gun away. It spins under a seat.

NOOR
You shot me.

RAFE
I shot at you. You moved.

NOOR
That's not an excuse.

DOC
Rafe, you've got a nicked lung. Breathe shallow.

RAFE
Easy for you.

DOC
Very easy. I'm not the one with a hole in him.

Noor lowers her pistol. Doc steps forward. Rafe lunges, grabs Noor's wrist, wrenches. The pistol clatters. They struggle, rolling across the floor, knocking over a rusted bucket. Doc shouts and dives in. The three of them grapple in the dust beneath a thousand painted stars.

DOC (CONT'D)
Stop! Both of you!

NOOR
Get off me!

RAFE
Let go!

Doc seizes the pistol. Points it at the ceiling. FIRES. Plaster rains. Pigeons erupt.

All three freeze.

DOC
Enough.

Nobody moves. Rafe lets go of her wrist. Noor wipes dust from her eyes.

NOOR
Doc. That was the last bullet.

DOC
I know.

He lowers the pistol. Sets it on the floor.

DOC (CONT'D)
Now let me look at both of you.

Rafe drops back. Noor sits beside him, breathing hard. Above, a comet crosses the dome.
